From b20f42e47a79e46a1fac617d5346578df7066858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:48:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] 1107 redfin: touch -> latch in stages
 (kern.sweet_touch_trace, default 1)

One touch event at a time is followed: sample IRQ time -> HID event dispatched
(SweetHID::touch) -> the swapper's first GPU submit after it (submit entry,
before the scanout gate) -> the first direct SwapEnd after that -> that swap's
or a later one's latch; abandoned after 200 ms. Per vsync notification also:
-> the swapper's first submit, -> its first SwapEnd (CA's tick-to-work time).
0.2 ms bins; 5 s line "SWEET TOUCH: 5s stages" with p50/p95 each. Try-lock
word, no locks taken; a few loads/stores per event. 0 = off.
---
